INPUT DOCUMENTATION v1 (identical across languages). Inputs are JSON objects. Integers below are JSON integers, not strings, floats or booleans. Arrays preserve order. The harness converts this wire representation to the run signature; this is not language syntax.
Fields: initial: integer in [0,1000000]; events: array of at most32 pairs [kind,amount]. kind is integer0=Credit(amount),1=Debit(amount),2=Lock,3=Unlock. amount is an integer in [-1000000,1000001]; for Lock/Unlock it is ignored. The pair encoding maps to Event values before run; it is not a tuple parameter passed directly to run.

Implement run(events,initial)->Summary(balance,rejected,peak,audit). Events have kinds Credit(amount), Debit(amount), Lock and Unlock. Start at initial balance, unlocked, rejected=0, peak=initial, empty audit. Credit/Debit amounts are valid iff 0<=amount<=83. Invalid amounts reject once and leave the balance unchanged. A valid credit always succeeds, even locked. A debit succeeds iff unlocked and amount<=balance; otherwise reject once. Zero-value credits/debits succeed under the same rules. Lock/Unlock are idempotent and never reject. After EVERY event append the current balance to audit, including rejects and locks. Peak is the maximum balance ever observed, including initial. Inputs: 0<=initial<=1000000, at most32 events, amounts between -1000000 and1000001; Lock/Unlock amounts are ignored. No overflow is possible.
Task family: ledger. Source-only comprehension. Return one JSON object: predictions (SIX complete normalized Summary objects for the inputs below); witness (any valid input yielding {"balance": 12, "rejected": 2, "peak": 17}; unspecified output fields can vary); direct_calls (application functions directly called by run, ignoring constructors/builtins/standard-library methods and util.reverse); impacted (functions in logic whose output can change for identical direct arguments if permitted changes its inclusive lower amount bound from0 to1; include the edited predicate itself); fault_location (the predicate responsible for that policy); counterexample (any valid input distinguishing original from that mutant). Use plain function names. Output byte values as lowercase hex. Optional top-level notes is a string. No tools. Return JSON only.
